WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.115
Some patterns repeat, over
and over. Other patterns grow.

2
00:00:08.335 --> 00:00:13.536
Find the part that repeats, or find the
step. Then you know what comes next.

3
00:00:14.036 --> 00:00:17.984
Here is a line of shapes.
Circle, square, circle, square.

4
00:00:18.204 --> 00:00:22.012
One small part comes round
again and again. Can you see it?

5
00:00:22.232 --> 00:00:25.901
Here it is. The part that
repeats is circle, square.

6
00:00:26.121 --> 00:00:30.765
It is two shapes long. Say it six
times and you have the whole line.

7
00:00:30.985 --> 00:00:37.811
Now a longer part: circle, square,
square. Three shapes, whole every time.

8
00:00:38.311 --> 00:00:41.609
Once you have found the part,
you can say what comes next.

9
00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:45.683
Circle, square, square, circle.
What shape comes after that?

10
00:00:45.903 --> 00:00:50.129
Square. The part tells you,
not the shape just before it.

11
00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:53.739
If a shape falls out of the
middle, the part mends it.

12
00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:57.722
Numbers make patterns too.
You count on in steps.

13
00:00:57.942 --> 00:01:02.540
Start at 3 and count on
in twos. 3, 5, 7, 9, 11.

14
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.289
Every jump is the same
size. You add 2 each time.

15
00:01:06.509 --> 00:01:11.432
You can start anywhere. 20,
25, 30, 35 goes up in fives.

16
00:01:11.932 --> 00:01:16.297
Now a number pattern. 15, 20,
25, 30. How does it go up?

17
00:01:16.517 --> 00:01:20.140
Look at the jumps between
them, not just at the numbers.

18
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.446
15 to 20 is 5. And 20 to 25 is 5 again.

19
00:01:24.666 --> 00:01:28.242
Always check two jumps. One
jump on its own can trick you.

20
00:01:28.462 --> 00:01:32.317
Every jump here is 5, so the
pattern goes up in fives.

21
00:01:32.537 --> 00:01:35.787
Now one number is hiding. 10, 20, gap, 40.

22
00:01:36.007 --> 00:01:38.840
It goes up in tens, so the gap must be 30.

23
00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.730
Counting back takes the
same step away each time.

24
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.409
Start at 50 and count back
in tens. 50, 40, 30, 20.

25
00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:51.576
The numbers get smaller. If one
gets bigger, you went the wrong way.

26
00:01:52.076 --> 00:01:55.141
Number patterns hide in
the hundred square as well.

27
00:01:55.361 --> 00:01:59.448
These coloured numbers
are 5, 15, 25 and 35.

28
00:01:59.668 --> 00:02:03.104
They go straight down one
column. Each one is ten more.

29
00:02:03.324 --> 00:02:07.968
So the next one is 45. Down
one row always adds ten.

30
00:02:08.468 --> 00:02:11.858
A repeating pattern has a
part that comes round again.

31
00:02:12.078 --> 00:02:15.840
A number pattern goes up,
or back, by the same step.

32
00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:19.682
You can count on in twos,
fives or tens, from any number.

33
00:02:19.902 --> 00:02:23.850
Find the step, and you can
always say what comes next.
